# Accounting, Monetary Math & Inventory Rules

## Mandatory decimal.js Invariant
- **Zero Native Floating-Point Math**: Native JavaScript operators (`+`, `-`, `*`, `/`) are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN on monetary values (prices, subtotals, taxes, discounts, balance due).
- Always import and use `Decimal` from `decimal.js`:
  ```typescript
  import Decimal from "decimal.js";
  const lineTotal = new Decimal(item.unitPrice).times(item.quantity);
  const tax = lineTotal.times(item.taxRate).dividedBy(100);
  const total = lineTotal.plus(tax).toFixed(2);
  ```
- All database columns for currency store `numeric(12, 2)`. Always format `Decimal` to string using `.toFixed(2)` before database persistence or JSON transmission.

## Indian GST Statutory Splits
- Ophthalmic prescription lenses: **5% GST** (HSN 9001).
- Spectacle frames, sunglasses, and accessories: **18% GST** (HSN 9003 / 9004).
- When a customer purchases a complete pair (Frame + Lens), calculate and display taxes independently per line item before summing into the final tax invoice.

## Atomic Inventory Concurrency Lock
- Never check stock in Node.js application memory prior to billing (TOCTOU race condition).
- Always decrement inventory atomically using SQL conditional updates with `RETURNING` inside `db.transaction()`:
  ```typescript
  const [updated] = await tx
    .update(inventoryItems)
    .set({ stockQuantity: sql`${inventoryItems.stockQuantity} - ${item.quantity}` })
    .where(
      and(
        eq(inventoryItems.id, item.inventoryItemId),
        eq(inventoryItems.organizationId, session.organizationId),
        sql`${inventoryItems.stockQuantity} >= ${item.quantity}`
      )
    )
    .returning({ id: inventoryItems.id });

  if (!updated) {
    throw new Error(`Insufficient stock for item: ${item.name}`);
  }
  ```
